Common Solution Approach

All three implementations solve the same problem: managing a list of tasks with the ability to add, remove and list of the tasks.
The common solution approach is encapsulating task management logic inside a single module structure thst can control access to the task lis.
Each implementations provides the same public operations AddTask, removeTask, listTask, while hiding how the tasks are sorted internally.

Similarities in structure

The main ides of this tasks are the same so because of this, their structures are also Similar. The Maintain a task collection using an array. Provided the three code methods
AddTask, removeTask, listTask. Even though they use different JavaScript constructs (object literal, constructor with prototype), each 
