Pattern vs Proto-Pattern Classification

Classification: Proto-Pattern 
This solution approach is best Classifiedd as a proto-pattern.

Why does it meet the Rule of Three?
Although the approach appears in three implementations, all examples exist within the same context and project.  
It has not yet been validated across multiple real-world applications or different problem domains.

What would be needed to make it a true pattern?

To become a true pattern, this approach would need at first use in multiple independent projects, second broader validation by other developers.

What are the characteristics of a proto-pattern that it exhibits?

This solution shows key proto-pattern characteristics. It is repeated multiple times, It solves a common and recurring problem, it demonstrates a consistent structure and behavior.


Conclusion
The three implementations demonstrate a consistent and reusable approach to task management.  
While they meet the Rule of Three in terms of repetition, the solution remains a proto-pattern due to limited validation beyond this context.